// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-004
// expect-error-at: 27:11
// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-004
// expect-error-at: 30:15
//
// WHAT IS STILL REFUSED, now that a general constant expression folds. The debt
// 0.6.4 paid was "must be a LITERAL"; it was never "must be VALID", and each site
// still owes its own check on what it got.
//
// A NAME FOLDS ONLY IF IT IS A MODULE-LEVEL `fixed` BINDING. This said "a `const`
// global", and that a `fixed` binding, "assigned once at RUN time", was correctly
// not one -- true until D-222 (2026-08-29) retired `const` and made every module
// binding a `fixed` one lowered to an LLVM `constant` with a compile-time
// initialiser (D-165), so a module `fixed` binding DOES fold. The file kept
// expecting a third refusal at `int32[RUNTIME_ONE]` for a month, and no runner
// noticed: the code was reported at the file's other two sites (the silent site
// D-332's count rule exists to catch, and caught). That line is ACCEPTED now, a
// control carrying no code; a local is still not a constant, and `comptime`
// still requires an expression that folds.
mod:not_constant;

fixed int32:RUNTIME_ONE = 1i32;

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    int32:local = 3i32;

    int32[local]:from_a_local;        // a local is not a constant
    int32[RUNTIME_ONE]:from_fixed;    // a module `fixed` binding folds (D-222): accepted

    int32:v = comptime(local + 1i32); // `comptime` requires one that folds
    exit 0i32;
};
